okay so the amazing spider-man 2 is a  film where the things surrounding it are  just as interesting as the movie itself  released in a time when the mcu was  really taking off it was critically  panned for having too many villains  subplots and a weird score that has the  singer basically giving electros in a  monologue garfield's web head had a  tough time from the beginning and his  version of peter parker was released  just five years after the toby maguire  incarnation before he himself was  replaced by holland's spider-man less  than 4 years after because of this the  amazing spider-man franchise is often  overlooked but it has picked up a strong  following online who absolutely loved  the film when you watch it you can kind  of see why too and though it has its low  points there's also a scene in it that i  think is absolutely perfect not that one  not not the one with jamie foxx making  himself a birthday cake from spider-man  no what i'm talking about is gwen  stacy's death ever since it was  announced that emma stone would be  playing the role in the amazing  spider-man we knew that the character  was truly doomed and this franchise very  much built up to that moment coming to  fruition for many years gwen's death was  viewed as a defining moment for the  character and though she's been brought  back to life in recent times for several  decades it was said that she should be a  character that remained dead like uncle  ben and the waynes gwen stacy's death  very much represents a number of things  in peter's life and to me the amazing  spider-man 2 absolutely nailed all of  these aspects peter parker is someone  who was plucked out of queens and given  incredible abilities that transformed  him into a superhuman  initially he wanted to use these gifts  for personal gain but after they  inadvertently led to the death of his  uncle ben he decided that he would  instead use them to help others peter  donned his spider-man costume to keep  those around him safe and he tried to  have a normal life being a vigilante  caused several runs with the law  including captain stacy stacy was killed  in the comics and the source material  had him saying in his final breath that  he should take care of gwen this  somewhat is the opposite to the amazing  spider-man franchise as cap was very  much like stay away from my daughter and  also like the video but either way you  look at it peter broke his promise  though he tried to keep gwen safe and  protector wanting things for his own  personal gain and happiness ultimately  led to him losing once more in the  comics green goblin took gwen to the top  of the brooklyn bridge and clocked her  with his glider which sent her hurtling  over the edge reacting quickly peter  fired a web around her ankles in order  to catch her but upon climbing down he  realized that she was dead for many  years peter didn't know whether it was  the impact of the goblin or the whiplash  from the webbing that ended her life and  he spent a long time dealing with the  guilt over this it was revealed later in  the comics that it was indeed the  webbing that broke her neck but i've  always been someone who viewed peter as  doing the best he could in the situation  and to me the fault lay with norman i  was born for putting her in that  position peter being peter though he  very much blamed himself and believed  that because he chose to be spider-man  that he's the one who put the woman he  loved in danger there's definitely a  debate to be had there and that's what  makes the character so interesting he's  someone who will try and do the best he  can but even doing the best he can can  often mean that those he loves die  because of it peter parker is an  extremely flawed character that fails  like the rest of us and that's what  makes him so relatable now whatever you  think of the amazing spider-man movies i  think most people agree that peter and  gwen's relationship was the strongest  part of those films andrew garfield and  emma stone dated in real life and that  chemistry definitely comes across in the  characters who go back and forth  throughout the two movies peter very  much wrestles with whether to keep his  promise to captain stacy or to follow  his heart and to be with the woman that  he loves in the film gwen gets a chance  at another life in london and peter in  the end decides to go with her to  england however the happy moment is  ruined by electro who starts to drain  power from the city gwen's death is even  foreshadowed here as the two stand on  top of a bridge which is of course where  the character died in the comics peter  webbs went to a car in order to keep her  safe but she ends up joining him in  stopping the electrical enemy gwen is  just as much of a genius as peter well  well probably even smarter and she knows  the grid specs in and out making her a  valuable asset in trying to stop max  from playing the incy wincy spider on  peter's head they managed to stop him  and send him to the mcu which is when  the green goblin swoops in cackling i  absolutely love the screeching of the  glider and though dain dahan's goblin  gets a lot of crap i think using the  actor's face instead of having a mask  works really well after his father's  death harry learned that he was dying  from a debilitating disease and he tried  to reach out to spider-man in order to  help find a cure however getting a blood  sample from oscorp labs led him into  mutating even further and thus he sought  revenge gwen was very much caught in the  crossfire and as the two battled in the  clock tower she was left dangling by a  thread as the pair battled it out as all  the gears came crashing down we got a  brilliant moment in which her literal  lifeline was cut and this leads to her  arm dropping before the rest of her body  does i'm not sure if the physics behind  this are right but it's such a cool shot  that made me get butterflies in my  stomach the first time that i watched it  you really get that sinking feeling as  gwen starts to fall and peter leaps down  the tower after her throughout the  spider-verse films we've often seen the  usage of a reflection in the eyes of  either spider-man or venom in which  they're trying to stop someone from  falling to their death we really get the  desperation peter faces here and seeing  her reflected in his eyes very much  reflects how much she means to him  there's a lot of subtle iconography here  too such as the web peter shoots out to  her itself resembling a hand reaching  out to save her and he watches it fires  through the gears of barely managing to  catch her now her death is of course one  of the most famous in all comic book  history so we know what's coming but  when analyzing the scene the creative  team do an incredible job of using the  scoring setting to make us think there's  a chance that peter will save gwen just  as gwen falls they tune everything out  and leave a solitary piano so that we  can truly see how focused peter is on  saving her though he was just attempting  to stop the goblin this soul instrument  blocks out everything else and makes it  so that we too just focus on her the  gears also cover her at one point so  that we can't see gwen but these open up  as the web shoots down giving us the  idea that all the obstacles have cleared  out the way and that he's actually going  to save her unfortunately though as the  web hits her he grabs the pipe and this  causes it to tighten which whips her  head backwards this cracks off the  ground and the snap from it is even more  impactful than the one carried out by  thanos they completely cut the music and  all the other effects so that all you  hear is this sound and i remember it  shaking through the cinema when i saw it  for the first time add to this the clock  which two breaks symbolizing that gwen's  time is up and you have a lot of things  laced throughout the subtext that makes  this moment hit 10 times harder in the  aftermath of it you could hear a pin  drop and though we knew this was coming  it was completely devastating to see it  play out hammering this moment home is  andrew garfield who drops down and gives  a performance that reminded me of bambi  finding his mother dead there's just  something so innocent to it that it  makes it even more devastating as with a  lot of spider-man movies we end with a  funeral but something about this one  feels ever more personal we dealt with a  lot of characters dying around peter but  watching the montage of him at a grave  as the seasons pass makes it hit home 10  times harder this truly captures the  grief that he's going through and lets  us know how impactful this was  spider-man is someone who's often seen  as a kitty character who's somewhat  cartoonish because of his big eyes and  brightly coloured costumes however he  can really have moments like this that  are real gut punches that make you  realize the kind of battles that peter  is truly fighting not only does he have  to tackle super criminals but he also  has to deal with losing those around him  he's not a billionaire he's not  invincible and he's not someone who ever  has it easy added this he broke captain  stacy's promise and the guy is just  taking constant l's and that's not the  only thing he's breaking eh  sorry about that  really bad now peter even quits being  spider-man but in the end it's the  memory of gwen that brings him back  around in the final few scenes he speaks  to ant-may who's putting ben's stuff in  a box she says the heavier the box is  the lighter she feels which very much  speaks to the acceptance part of grief  and learning to let go though she isn't  chucking it out because it's part of her  she's finding a better place for it  peter plays gwen's graduation speech in  which he's told to hold on to hope and  to become that she says that even if we  fail to try and become that which very  much summarizes her death and peter's  next step much like may he puts gwen's  possessions in a box but leaves one  photo behind as a reminder and he  returns his spider-man say what you want  about the film but i feel like this rise  and fall of the character represents why  we as audiences love him so much he is a  person who's been through some of the  worst things imaginable and though he's  lost people close to him he will still  come back every time gwen's death is  obviously a tragedy but it's such an  intrinsic part of the character that  shows his greatest strength is dealing  with his own failures and coming back  from them though i do have some issues  with the film i think gwen's death is  one of the most impactful scenes in a  comic book movie ever and that's why  that scene is absolutely perfect  now obviously i'd love to hear your  thoughts on it so make sure you comment  below and let me know we are running a  competition right now and giving away  three copies of the spider-man 4k  trilogies on the 30th of december all  you have to do to be on the chance of  winning is like the video make sure you  subscribe with notifications on and drop  a comment below with your thoughts on  the scene we picked the comments at  random at the end of the month and the  winners of the last one are on screen  right now so if that's you then message  me on twitter heavyspoilers if you want  something else to watch then make sure  you check out our breakdown of spiderman  no way home which will be linked on  screen right now we've talked about all  the tv spots all the trailers so it's  definitely worth checking out right  after this without the way thank you for  singing through the video i've been poor  i'll see you in the next one take care  peace
 

